# SPA fallbacks, listed explicitly. There is deliberately NO /* catch-all.
#
# A top-level 404.html now exists, which switches Pages out of its default
# single-page-application mode. That default was what answered a missing
# asset with index.html as text/html: the browser rejected it as a module
# script AND cached it under the .js URL for that asset's max-age (4h), so
# a deploy-window propagation gap left visitors on a blank page long after
# the server recovered. With 404.html present, a miss is a real 404 - it
# fails once and recovers on reload instead of poisoning a cache.
#
# The trade-off: Pages no longer falls back for us, so every client-side
# route MUST be listed here or it will 404. Both slash forms are listed
# rather than relying on Pages' trailing-slash normalisation.

# Portfolio (react-router)
/about /index.html 200
/about/ /index.html 200
/apps /index.html 200
/apps/ /index.html 200
/video /index.html 200
/video/ /index.html 200
/blogs /index.html 200
/blogs/ /index.html 200

# Integricare - hand-rolled routing on window.location.pathname
/integricare/about /integricare/index.html 200
/integricare/about/ /integricare/index.html 200
/integricare/course/* /integricare/index.html 200
/integricare/blog/* /integricare/index.html 200

